From: =?UTF-8?q?S=C3=A9bastien=20Celles?= <s.celles@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 7 Jun 2026 13:32:34 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 47/62] verimark: try 17-byte 0x96 03 commit on IT (sub-cmd +
 TUID, no SID)

1-byte payload returned 0x0504 (vs 0x0404 with the DT 123-byte
payload). The status change tells us the IT firmware does NOT
reject the request as out-of-state with the shorter form ; it
just complains about something missing. Next smallest natural
shape : sub-command + TUID only, drop the SID + footer that the
DT carries. 17 bytes total.
---
 libfprint/drivers/verimark/verimark.c | 16 ++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/libfprint/drivers/verimark/verimark.c b/libfprint/drivers/verimark/verimark.c
index ac2e73b..4c22873 100644
--- a/libfprint/drivers/verimark/verimark.c
+++ b/libfprint/drivers/verimark/verimark.c
@@ -2583,12 +2583,16 @@ enroll_sm_run_state(FpiSsm *ssm, FpDevice *dev)
         const gboolean is_it = (usb != NULL &&
                                 g_usb_device_get_pid(usb) == VERIMARK_PID_IT);
         if (is_it) {
-            /* Minimal payload : just the sub-command byte 0x03 = commit.
-             * The DT's 123-byte body (TUID + SID + footer) was rejected
-             * with 0x0404 on the IT. Try the smallest valid framing
-             * first ; we can grow it incrementally if needed. */
-            static const uint8_t it_commit_payload[1] = { 0x03 };
-            fp_warn("verimark: IT enroll sending 0x96 03 with 1-byte payload");
+            /* 1-byte payload gave 0x0504 (vs 0x0404 from DT 123-byte) —
+             * progress, but still rejected. Next hypothesis : the IT
+             * commit just needs sub-cmd + TUID, no SID footer. Build
+             * [0x03][TUID 16B] = 17 bytes. */
+            uint8_t it_commit_payload[17];
+            it_commit_payload[0] = 0x03;
+            memcpy(it_commit_payload + 1, ctx->new_tuid,
+                   VERIMARK_STORAGE_TUID_LEN);
+            fp_warn("verimark: IT enroll sending 0x96 03 with 17-byte payload "
+                    "(sub-cmd + 16B TUID)");
             verimark_session_call_opcode_async(&self->session, self->transport,
                 3000, 0x96, it_commit_payload, sizeof(it_commit_payload),
                 cancel, enr_cb_commit, ssm);
